    "q-182352": {
      "dom_id": "step-q182352",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Find the missing values in the following truth table:\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,¬P∨¬Q\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-4}} |",
      "worked_solution": "First, we add the columns for $¬P$ and $¬Q,$ \nwhere the truth values are opposite to the corresponding values in the columns for $P$ and $Q,$ respectively.\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,¬P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,¬Q\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nThen, we add a column for $¬P∨¬Q.$ Remember that $¬P∨¬Q$ is true if either $¬P$ is true or $¬Q$ is true.\n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,¬P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,¬Q\\,$ | $\\,¬P∨¬Q\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
